From 74ece4487d67461367e3c32c1e0ee4d57382cb98 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jiaxing Hu <gahing@gahingwoo.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 15:26:45 +1200
Subject: [PATCH] rocket RK3576: derive DPU 0x4050 for depthwise instead of
 hardcoding it

Its SIZE_E_2 field, bits 10 to 8, counts 16-channel atomics. Compiling vendor
.rknn files at ten channel counts and reading 0x4050 out of each gives

    channels    16   32   48   64   80   96  112  128  256 1024
    SIZE_E_2     0    1    2    3    0    1    2    3    3    3

    SIZE_E_2 = (DIV_ROUND_UP(oc, 16) - 1) & 3

Seven of those were fitted and three were predicted before being compiled: 16
and 80 give 0, a value none of the fitted points showed, and 112 gives 2.

This file hardcoded 0x00013133, which is the 32 channel case, so every
depthwise whose channel count is not 32, 96, 160 and so on was configured with
the wrong one. Every depthwise this project tests has 32 channels except the
1024 channel layer that does not work, which is why it never showed.

ROCKET_DW_OW_CFG forces a value; setting it to 0x00013133 restores the old
constant as a control. At 32 channels the expression gives back exactly that,
so the layers that already pass cannot move.

Signed-off-by: Jiaxing Hu <gahing@gahingwoo.com>
---
 src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_regcmd.c | 24 +++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_regcmd.c b/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_regcmd.c
index bc4b70c..192cc58 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_regcmd.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_regcmd.c
@@ -668,7 +668,29 @@ fill_regcmd_rk3576_normal(struct rkt_ml_subgraph *subgraph,
     * conv2d-cal and wrong for every conv with 16, 48, 80, 112 or 144 output
     * channels. ROCKET_DPU4050_CONST=1 restores it as a control.
     */
-   R_DPU(0x4050, dw ? 0x00013133
+   /*
+    * The depthwise value is NOT a constant either: its SIZE_E_2 field, bits
+    * 10 to 8, counts 16-channel atomics.
+    *
+    * Compiling vendor .rknn files at ten channel counts from 16 to 1024 and
+    * reading 0x4050 out of each gives 0, 1, 2, 3, 0, 1, 2, 3, 3, 3 in that
+    * field for 16, 32, 48, 64, 80, 96, 112, 128, 256 and 1024, which is
+    *
+    *     SIZE_E_2 = (DIV_ROUND_UP(oc, 16) - 1) & 3
+    *
+    * on all ten. Seven of those were fitted and three were PREDICTED before
+    * being compiled: 16 and 80 give 0, a value the fitted points never showed,
+    * and 112 gives 2. This driver hardcoded 0x00013133, which is the 32
+    * channel case, so every depthwise with a channel count outside 32, 96, 160
+    * and so on was configured with the wrong one.
+    *
+    * ROCKET_DW_OW_CFG forces a value, and setting it to 0x00013133 restores
+    * the old constant as the control.
+    */
+   uint32_t dw_ow = 0x00013033 |
+                    ((uint32_t)((DIV_ROUND_UP(oc, 16) - 1) & 3) << 8);
+
+   R_DPU(0x4050, dw ? rkt_env_u32("ROCKET_DW_OW_CFG", dw_ow)
                     : (getenv("ROCKET_DPU4050_CONST") || (oc % 32) == 0
                           ? 0x80011111 : 0x80011011));
    /*
-- 
